narrative:
## A Mini Text Adventure Engine

A text adventure has rooms, actions, and a game state that tracks where you are and what you carry.

### The Room Enum

```xiom
enum Room {
  Kitchen,
  Garden,
  Bedroom,
  Attic,
}
```

### The Action Enum

```xiom
enum Action {
  Go(room: Room),
  Look,
  Take(item: Str),
  Quit,
}
```

`Go` carries the destination room. `Take` carries the item name. `Look` and `Quit` need no extra data.

### The GameState Struct

```xiom
type GameState = {
  current_room: Room;
  has_key: Bool;
}
```

### Processing Actions

```xiom
fn process(state: GameState, action: Action) -> Str {
  match action {
    Go(room) => {
      current_room = room;
      return "You walk to the " + room_name(room) + ".";
    }
    Look => { return "You are in the " + room_name(current_room) + "."; }
    Take(item) => {
      if item == "key" && current_room == Room.Kitchen {
        has_key = true;
        return "You picked up the key.";
      }
      return "There is no " + item + " here.";
    }
    Quit => { return "Goodbye!"; }
  }
}
```

### Playing the Game

```xiom
var state = GameState{ current_room: Room.Kitchen; has_key: false; };

process(state, Action.Look);                        // "You are in the kitchen."
process(state, Action.Go(Room.Garden));              // "You walk to the garden."
process(state, Action.Go(Room.Kitchen));             // "You walk to the kitchen."
process(state, Action.Take("key"));                  // "You picked up the key."
```

